{"company_id":"confluence-sh","company_name":"Confluence Labs","website":"https://confluence.sh","source":"yc","items":[{"id":"ev_877cfc8d213a","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"seed_metadata","url":"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/confluence-labs","title":"yc seed metadata","text_snippet":"AI models that learn from experience\nIndustries: B2B\nBatch: Winter 2026\nTeam size (listed): 2\n{\"slug\": \"confluence-labs\", \"status\": \"Active\", \"team_size\": 2, \"regions\": [\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"], \"all_locations\": \"San Francisco, CA, USA\", \"isHiring\": false, \"top_company\": false, \"objectID\": \"31162\", \"founders_page_fetched\": true}","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:23.818418Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"source":"yc","program":"YC"}},{"id":"ev_8a330b4e3545","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"homepage","url":"https://www.confluence.sh/","title":"Confluence Labs","text_snippet":"Confluence Labs Confluence Labs AI models that learn from experience. Confluence Labs is an AI research lab focused on learning efficiency – how quickly can you learn something given a limited amount of data / fewest number of experiments. Many of humanity's biggest advances are locked behind a certain number of experiments. The strongest examples are drug and materials discovery. The right drugs could essentially end human disease. The right materials could unlock fusion or help end global warming. These are constrained search problems where a certain number of experiments can unlock a breakthrough for humanity and change the world. The mission of our company and of our research is to enable people to hit those breakthroughs in the fewest number of experiments possible, accelerating and enabling scientific technologies. Writing Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 Reach out at founders@confluence.sh . Made by Brent and Niranjan Backed by Y Combinator and Paul Graham","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/8e44243c41e83112.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:24.044921Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{}},{"id":"ev_2114b34dac4d","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://www.confluence.sh","title":"Confluence Labs","text_snippet":"Title: Confluence Labs\n# Confluence Labs. An AI research lab focused on learning efficiency. While modern AI excels in any area you can collect a lot of data for, it struggles in areas where data is sparse or costly to attain. Designing new molecules, discovering new physics, engineering new materials, and even developing more effective systems of governance are all domains where collecting data is extremely costly. We dream of a world where AI accelerates research in all of these domains and creates a more abundant future for humanity, but the current technology is not there. That's why we started Confluence Labs. ## Our Approach – Learning Efficiency. Learning efficiency is the core focus of Confluence Labs. We split it into two things. 1. **Experimental design:** How can we ask the right questions? The \"right\" experiment to run is the one that gets you to your goal fastest. We want to maximize learning delta and minimize the total number of experiments. 2. **Data efficiency:** How can we maximally learn from the data we already have? We're backed by **Y Combinator**, and looking for scientists and research labs to collaborate with. If you're working in a data-sparse domain and excited about AI collaborating with humans on research, please reach out!","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:28.927390Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_076c21848f78","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://confluence.sh","title":"Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2","text_snippet":"Confluence Labs is coming out of stealth with **SOTA on ARC-AGI-2** with a score of **97.9%** at **$11.77 per task** on the public eval. ARC-AGI-2 is a benchmark that tests an AI system's ability to solve novel reasoning tasks from just a few examples. We take the latest models and allow them to find the optimal solution by directing them to write code which describes the transformation represented by a particular ARC problem. ## ARC-AGI-2 is Saturated – What Does This Mean for the World? ARC is a data efficiency benchmark. Typical approaches to ARC-AGI have struggled because modern ML excels in areas where you can collect a lot of training data, but struggles in areas where data is sparse or costly to attain. We think LLMs can be used in combination with discrete modeling to assist humans in data-sparse domains. 2. **Data-Efficient Modeling** – By pushing the capabilities of both LLMs and discrete program search, we can make predictions with far less data and accelerate frontier research.","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:28.927435Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_c95bcbaf3e78","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs","title":"Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2","text_snippet":"Confluence Labs is coming out of stealth with **SOTA on ARC-AGI-2** with a score of **97.9%** at **~$12 per task** on the public eval. ARC-AGI-2 is a benchmark that tests an AI system's ability to solve novel reasoning tasks from just a few examples. We take the latest models and allow them to find the optimal solution by directing them to write code which describes the transformation represented by a particular ARC problem. ## ARC-AGI-2 is Saturated – What Does This Mean for the World? ARC is a data efficiency benchmark. Typical approaches to ARC-AGI have struggled because modern ML excels in areas where you can collect a lot of training data, but struggles in areas where data is sparse or costly to attain. We think LLMs can be used in combination with discrete modeling to assist humans in data-sparse domains. 2. **Data-Efficient Modeling** – By pushing the capabilities of both LLMs and discrete program search, we can make predictions with far less data and accelerate frontier research.","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:28.927461Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_2e90ecc339a2","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"fallback_page","url":"https://www.confluence.sh","title":"Confluence Labs","text_snippet":"Confluence Labs Confluence Labs AI models that learn from experience. Confluence Labs is an AI research lab focused on learning efficiency – how quickly can you learn something given a limited amount of data / fewest number of experiments. Many of humanity's biggest advances are locked behind a certain number of experiments. The strongest examples are drug and materials discovery. The right drugs could essentially end human disease. The right materials could unlock fusion or help end global warming. These are constrained search problems where a certain number of experiments can unlock a breakthrough for humanity and change the world. The mission of our company and of our research is to enable people to hit those breakthroughs in the fewest number of experiments possible, accelerating and enabling scientific technologies. Writing Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 Reach out at founders@confluence.sh . Made by Brent and Niranjan Backed by Y Combinator and Paul Graham","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/3e1c2fc003979e9e.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:29.026941Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"search_query":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_dc9c3d2e2e60","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"fallback_page","url":"https://confluence.sh","title":"Confluence Labs","text_snippet":"Confluence Labs Confluence Labs AI models that learn from experience. Confluence Labs is an AI research lab focused on learning efficiency – how quickly can you learn something given a limited amount of data / fewest number of experiments. Many of humanity's biggest advances are locked behind a certain number of experiments. The strongest examples are drug and materials discovery. The right drugs could essentially end human disease. The right materials could unlock fusion or help end global warming. These are constrained search problems where a certain number of experiments can unlock a breakthrough for humanity and change the world. The mission of our company and of our research is to enable people to hit those breakthroughs in the fewest number of experiments possible, accelerating and enabling scientific technologies. Writing Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 Reach out at founders@confluence.sh . Made by Brent and Niranjan Backed by Y Combinator and Paul Graham","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/8e44243c41e83112.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:29.035687Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"search_query":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_f56c772dca05","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"fallback_page","url":"https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs","title":"Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2","text_snippet":"Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 ← Confluence Labs Introducing Confluence Labs AI models that learn from experience. Confluence Labs is coming out of stealth with SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 with a score of 97.9% at ~$12 per task on the public eval. This is how we did it, why it matters, and what's next. ARC-AGI-2 is a benchmark that tests an AI system's ability to solve novel reasoning tasks from just a few examples. It's considered one of the hardest AI benchmarks in the world. As recently as a year ago, even the best models scored in the single digits. Score vs Cost per Task on the public evaluation set — data source We've open sourced our SOTA solver. You can reproduce our results here . Our Approach – Program Synthesis driven by LLMs LLMs are exceedingly good at writing code. We take the latest models and allow them to find the optimal solution by directing them to write code which describes the transformation represented by a particular ARC problem. The principles of our approach can be boiled down to a few key ideas: Structure the problem such that it optimally resembles the underlying LLM's training data Enable long-horizon work on the problem so a model can continue to build on its past work Precisely structure the criteria of the solution and give the model a way to measure that ARC-AGI-2 is Saturated – What Does This Mean for the World? ARC is a data efficiency benchmark. It measures how well you can make a prediction based on a few examples. Typical approaches to ARC-AGI have struggled because modern ML excels in areas where you can collect a lot of training data, but struggles in areas where data is sparse or costly to attain. We think LLMs can be used in combination with discrete modeling to assist humans in data-sparse domains. We're most excited about the application of this to meaningful and challenging frontiers such as hardware engineering, drug design, and physics research. What Does This Mean for Us? Our core belief is that learning efficie","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/5884d4324f0930dc.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:29.161212Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"search_query":"Confluence Labs site:confluence.sh hiring","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_646a832eeb9f","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/flock%20safety/9baaeda3-3dcc-4a0e-a3b1-e7dd31d6615c","title":"Senior Hardware Solutions Engineer @ Flock - Jobs","text_snippet":"Experience with documentation tools like Confluence is a plus. Ability to work effectively with cross-functional teams, including QA and engineering. Strong","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:30.180812Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:ashbyhq.com","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_195384f82377","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/makai-labs/96a66a83-85d5-4e06-a575-92139f4ee3b3","title":"Production Support Analyst @ Makai Labs - Jobs","text_snippet":"Experience using or willingness to learn ticketing and collaboration tools (e.g., Jira, Zendesk, ServiceNow, Linear, Slack, Confluence/Notion, etc.). Strong","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:30.180853Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:ashbyhq.com","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_cf8d27c3c260","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/fluidstack/18af0603-cead-4bca-8dd0-0b95ea6a2cf8","title":"Data Center Project Manager - Construction @ Fluidstack - Jobs","text_snippet":"Expert user of scheduling (P6/Project), cost (Procore, Ares, Excel) and collaboration (Smartsheet, Confluence) tools. Excellent written and verbal communication","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:30.180865Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"Confluence Labs site:ashbyhq.com","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_c994edaca6d1","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"careers","url":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/flock%20safety/9baaeda3-3dcc-4a0e-a3b1-e7dd31d6615c","title":"Senior Hardware Solutions Engineer @ Flock","text_snippet":"Senior Hardware Solutions Engineer @ Flock","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/8b554ad1a427ca0b.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:30.649302Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"discovered_via":"search","query_used":"Confluence Labs site:ashbyhq.com"}},{"id":"ev_ab5eb3d2e2d2","company_id":"confluence-sh","source_type":"blog","url":"https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs","title":"Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2","text_snippet":"Introducing Confluence Labs – SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 ← Confluence Labs Introducing Confluence Labs AI models that learn from experience. Confluence Labs is coming out of stealth with SOTA on ARC-AGI-2 with a score of 97.9% at ~$12 per task on the public eval. This is how we did it, why it matters, and what's next. ARC-AGI-2 is a benchmark that tests an AI system's ability to solve novel reasoning tasks from just a few examples. It's considered one of the hardest AI benchmarks in the world. As recently as a year ago, even the best models scored in the single digits. Score vs Cost per Task on the public evaluation set — data source We've open sourced our SOTA solver. You can reproduce our results here . Our Approach – Program Synthesis driven by LLMs LLMs are exceedingly good at writing code. We take the latest models and allow them to find the optimal solution by directing them to write code which describes the transformation represented by a particular ARC problem. The principles of our approach can be boiled down to a few key ideas: Structure the problem such that it optimally resembles the underlying LLM's training data Enable long-horizon work on the problem so a model can continue to build on its past work Precisely structure the criteria of the solution and give the model a way to measure that ARC-AGI-2 is Saturated – What Does This Mean for the World? ARC is a data efficiency benchmark. It measures how well you can make a prediction based on a few examples. Typical approaches to ARC-AGI have struggled because modern ML excels in areas where you can collect a lot of training data, but struggles in areas where data is sparse or costly to attain. We think LLMs can be used in combination with discrete modeling to assist humans in data-sparse domains. We're most excited about the application of this to meaningful and challenging frontiers such as hardware engineering, drug design, and physics research. What Does This Mean for Us? Our core belief is that learning efficiency is the key bottleneck to solving the world's hardest problems. We think AI can help in data-sparse domains, and we're approaching this from 2 angles: Hypothesis generation – A hypothesis is a testable prediction about the world. If you optimally generate hypotheses, the results of your experiments are maximally informative, and you can reduce the time it takes to develop a new technology or solve a hard problem. Data-Efficient Modeling – By pushing the capabilities of both LLMs and discrete program search, we can make predictions with far less data and accelerate frontier research. What's Next? We're going hard on developing our core technology, building out the team, and developing partnerships with researchers and engineers. We're looking for collaborators in hardware engineering, biology, materials science, and other fields where progress is gated by the cost of physical experiments. If that sounds like you, reach out at founders@confluence.sh . Made by Brent and Niranjan Backed by Y Combinator and Paul Graham","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/confluence-sh/5884d4324f0930dc.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:31.521057Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{}}],"coverage":{"homepage_found":true,"careers_found":true,"docs_found":false,"status_found":false,"blog_or_changelog_found":true,"github_found":false,"seed_metadata_found":true,"fallback_search_used":true,"total_successful_sources":6,"source_diversity_score":0.5,"confidence_cap":"high"},"trace":{"probes_attempted":["seed_metadata","homepage","known_links","careers","docs","status","blog_changelog","github","agent_search_fallback"],"urls_attempted":["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/confluence-labs","https://www.confluence.sh/","https://www.confluence.sh","https://confluence.sh","https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs","https://www.confluence.sh","https://confluence.sh","https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/flock%20safety/9baaeda3-3dcc-4a0e-a3b1-e7dd31d6615c","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/makai-labs/96a66a83-85d5-4e06-a575-92139f4ee3b3","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/fluidstack/18af0603-cead-4bca-8dd0-0b95ea6a2cf8","https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/flock%20safety/9baaeda3-3dcc-4a0e-a3b1-e7dd31d6615c","https://www.confluence.sh/blog/introducing-confluence-labs"],"failures":[],"cache_hits":0,"tool_calls":17}}
{"company_id":"mochacare-com","company_name":"MochaCare","website":"https://www.mochacare.com","source":"yc","items":[{"id":"ev_846d225059a3","company_id":"mochacare-com","source_type":"seed_metadata","url":"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/mochacare","title":"yc seed metadata","text_snippet":"Agentic Management Service for Care Organizations\nIndustries: B2B, Operations\nBatch: Winter 2026\nTeam size (listed): 2\n{\"slug\": \"mochacare\", \"status\": \"Active\", \"team_size\": 2, \"regions\": [\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"], \"all_locations\": \"San Francisco, CA, USA\", \"isHiring\": true, \"top_company\": false, \"objectID\": \"31269\", \"founders_page_fetched\": true}","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:41.464491Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"source":"yc","program":"YC"}},{"id":"ev_0222c45a1b80","company_id":"mochacare-com","source_type":"homepage","url":"https://www.mochacare.com","title":"MochaCare","text_snippet":"MochaCare MochaCare Book Demo Supported by the investors of Supported by the investors of Airbnb Care Organization Operations, Managed. Human Virtual Assistants Supercharged by AI for Care Agencies, Facilities, and More Hiring, scheduling, client intake, and growth insights. Book Demo Real humans + AI tools, awake 24/7 to support you Meet Nick & Pranav → Built by a Team From How we help you grow Use one or both — they work great together. Solution #1: Mocha Managed Ops & growth team, on call. ✓ After-hours, weekends, holidays — you choose ✓ We handle scheduling, hiring, or both ✓ Nick & Pranav personally on call ✓ AI insights to show where to focus for growth Learn more Solution #2: Mocha Tools AI tools to scale your team. ✓ AI scheduling & recruiting automations ✓ Applicant tracking system (ATS) ✓ Connects your existing systems ✓ Works alongside Mocha Managed Learn more Solution #1: Mocha Managed We handle hiring, scheduling, or both, while unlocking growth Mocha AI Handles the mundane Missed clock-ins/clock-outs, availability updates, shift notes — done automatically. Our Team Handles human touch Emergencies, hiring top candidates, client concerns — addressed immediately. 24/7 monitoring through our internal dashboard: Live monitoring URGENT HIRE URGENT HIRE 6:12 AM New applicant: Brenna Adams is a top 5% candidate. Reach out immediately to close her before competitors do. Nick is calling EMERGENCY SCHEDULING EMERGENCY 6:01 AM Mrs. Johnson called. Her caregiver didn’t show up for the 6 AM shift. Mocha AI found 3 available substitutes. Pranav is calling the family ROUTINE ROUTINE 5:52 AM Caregiver Sarah Franklin called to clock out from Mrs. Park’s shift. WellSky updated and shift notes added. Handled by Mocha AI Set our hours and get back to growing. 1 You set our hours 2 We personalize to you 3 Your agency grows Led by former caregivers with tech backgrounds from Stanford, Microsoft, Spotify. Meet us → Solution #2: Mocha Tools Our AI tools The AI platform behind Mocha Managed, available as standalone software for your team. Hiring running on autopilot. Hiring on autopilot. The first AI-powered ATS for home care. Configure your hiring pipeline, collect required docs, and let AI agents move candidates through every step—on autopilot. ✓ AI or human interviews—you choose ✓ Indeed integration or custom forms ✓ Auto-collect TB tests, HCA status, licenses ✓ Automated reminders & follow-ups See our AI Recruiter → i Indeed Custom Form MochaCare ATS AI-Powered 3 new applicants added Sync from Indeed or use our custom application form AI Interviewer ✓ Available anytime ✓ Consistent screening ✓ Instant scheduling OR/AND Human Interviewer Auto schedules ✓ Personal touch ✓ Culture fit assessment ✓ Auto-scheduled by AI MochaCare AI Document Collection Hi Maria! Please upload your TB test and driver's license to complete your application. Hi Maria! Please upload your TB test and license. M TB_Test.pdf License.jpg Delivered March 2024 All Shifts Filled M T W T F S S 18 19 20 21 22 23 24 Lisa K. canceled Wed shift Finding Coverage... SM Sarah M. 98% match JK James K. 94% match ML Maria L. 89% match ✓ Schedule Status All shifts covered for today Schedule coverage 24/7. When a caregiver calls out—even after hours—Mocha identifies perfect caregiver matches based on your agency's preferences, then instantly calls or texts them to fill the shift. See After-Hours Scheduling → Shift management 24/7. Mocha reminds caregivers of upcoming shifts and care plans. When session notes, clock-ins, or clock-outs are forgotten, Mocha reaches out to fill in the gaps. See Shift Management in Action → Shift Activity Action Needed Today's Shift - Mrs. Johnson Clock-out Missing ! Notes Missing ! Session Notes No notes recorded... Sarah M. . . . Calling On call with Sarah Collecting shift info Connected Sarah M. ⚠️ Missing Information Clock-out and notes missing Coming Soon Visibility that drives growth. Mocha surfaces the right data at the right time to identify and enable you to capitalize on opportunities for agency growth. Learn More → New Family Referral Doctor Lawyer Caregiver Facility \"Mrs. Chen has Parkinson's, 3 similar families served\" \"Family mentioned attorney James Li, potential referral partner\" \"Dr. Patel referred 4 families this quarter, send thank you\" \"Intake conversion dropped 15%, review follow-up timing\" \"Sunrise Assisted Living sent 3 referrals this month, schedule check-in\" \"Caregiver Sarah suggested Jamie for interviews, schedule screening\" We build custom integrations into your systems. We connect to your software so our team can schedule like your best coordinator. Don't see yours? Let us know. Stop reacting. Start growing. MochaCare handles your ops, connects your data, and gives your team insights to build predictable, sustainable growth. Talk to us and see how. Talk to Nick & Pranav MochaCare Backed by Y Combinator Your team for home care scheduling, interviewing, and growth. Human-led, AI-powered, from San Francisco. Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions SMS Terms Contact Us","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/mochacare-com/31c37863b6afde86.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:41.643109Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{}},{"id":"ev_c7a4a3c95bdb","company_id":"mochacare-com","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://www.mochacare.com/sms-terms","title":"MochaCare","text_snippet":"Text messages and calls may be sent in two ways: MochaCare may contact Agency Customers directly with platform alerts and notifications, and Agency Customers may send messages to their caregivers, job applicants, and staff (\"End Users\") using MochaCare's messaging tools. **Agency Customers:** By signing up for and using MochaCare, Agency Customer staff consent to receive SMS messages and calls from MochaCare related to platform alerts, account notifications, urgent staffing updates, and other operational communications. **End Users:** By providing your phone number to a home care agency that uses MochaCare — whether through a job application form, onboarding process, or other opt-in method — you consent to receive SMS messages from that agency sent through the MochaCare platform. **Messages from MochaCare to Agency Customers** may include: platform alerts and system notifications; urgent staffing updates (such as caregiver cancellations or no-shows); account and billing notifications; security alerts; and other operational communications related to their use of the Service.","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:45.233878Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"site:mochacare.com jobs","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_6053fb82100a","company_id":"mochacare-com","source_type":"search_result","url":"https://www.mochacare.com/privacy","title":"MochaCare","text_snippet":"We use information for the following purposes: to provide, operate, and maintain our platform for Agency Customers; to process data on behalf of Agency Customers, including managing hiring pipelines, facilitating AI-powered and human interviews, and storing compliance documents; to enable Agency Customers to send operational communications (including SMS messages) to their caregivers and applicants through our platform; to improve, personalize, and expand our Service; to provide customer support to Agency Customers; to detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or technical issues; and to comply with legal obligations. We may share personal information in the following circumstances: with Agency Customers, who own and control the End User data collected through our platform; with sub-processors and service providers who assist us in operating our platform (such as cloud hosting, communication, and analytics providers) under contractual obligations to protect data; if required by law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request; to enforce our terms of service or protect the rights, property, or safety of MochaCare, our customers, or the public; and with consent or at the direction of the Agency Customer.","raw_cache_path":null,"fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:45.233902Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"query_used":"site:mochacare.com jobs","search_provider":"tavily"}},{"id":"ev_5b7e7fbfc77d","company_id":"mochacare-com","source_type":"careers","url":"https://www.mochacare.com/sms-terms","title":"MochaCare","text_snippet":"MochaCare MochaCare Book Demo SMS Terms of Service Last updated: February 8, 2026 1. Overview MochaCare provides a software platform that home care agencies (\"Agency Customers\") use to manage their staffing operations. Text messages and calls may be sent in two ways: MochaCare may contact Agency Customers directly with platform alerts and notifications, and Agency Customers may send messages to their caregivers, job applicants, and staff (\"End Users\") using MochaCare's messaging tools. These SMS Terms of Service describe how text messaging and calling works on the MochaCare platform. 2. Consent to Receive Messages Agency Customers: By signing up for and using MochaCare, Agency Customer staff consent to receive SMS messages and calls from MochaCare related to platform alerts, account notifications, urgent staffing updates, and other operational communications. SMS consent is not a condition of purchasing any goods or services. End Users: By providing your phone number to a home care agency that uses MochaCare — whether through a job application form, onboarding process, or other opt-in method — you consent to receive SMS messages from that agency sent through the MochaCare platform. Your consent is provided to the Agency Customer, not to MochaCare directly. SMS consent is not a condition of employment or of purchasing any goods or services. 3. Types of Messages Messages from MochaCare to Agency Customers may include: platform alerts and system notifications; urgent staffing updates (such as caregiver cancellations or no-shows); account and billing notifications; security alerts; and other operational communications related to their use of the Service. Messages from Agency Customers to End Users (sent through MochaCare) may include: new shift availability and assignment notifications; shift coverage and replacement requests; interview scheduling confirmations and reminders; job application status updates; document submission reminders for compliance items such as certifications and licenses; and responses to inquiries or HELP requests. 4. Message Frequency Message frequency varies depending on your role and the Agency Customer's use of the platform. Caregivers with active shift schedules may receive multiple messages per week. Job applicants typically receive messages during the application and onboarding process. Messages sent through MochaCare are operational and staffing-related — Agency Customers do not use our platform to send marketing or promotional messages. 5. Message and Data Rates Message and data rates may apply. Neither MochaCare nor the Agency Customer charges you for receiving SMS messages, but your mobile carrier may charge you for sending and receiving text messages. Please contact your carrier for details about your messaging plan. 6. Opt-Out You can opt out of receiving SMS messages at any time by replying STOP to any message you receive. After opting out, you will receive a confirmation message and will no longer receive text messages through the MochaCare platform. To opt back in at any time, reply START . Please note that opting out of SMS messages may affect your ability to receive time-sensitive shift notifications and other important operational communications from the home care agency you work with. You may want to inform your agency if you opt out so they can reach you through alternative channels. 7. Help For assistance with text messages, reply HELP to any message. You can also contact the home care agency that sent you the message directly. If you need to reach MochaCare, email us at support@mochacare.com or visit www.mochacare.com . 8. Privacy Your privacy is important to us. MochaCare processes End User phone numbers and messaging data on behalf of Agency Customers. We do not sell, rent, or share End User phone numbers or SMS opt-in consent with third parties for marketing purposes. Your information is used solely for the staffing and operational purposes described in our Privacy Policy . 9. Supported Carriers Our SMS service is supported by major US carriers including AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile, and other participating carriers. Carrier support may vary, and neither MochaCare nor the Agency Customer is responsible for delayed or undelivered messages due to carrier issues. 10. Changes to These Terms We may update these SMS Terms of Service from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated date. Your continued receipt of SMS messages after any changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated terms. 11. Contact Us If you have any questions about these SMS Terms of Service, please contact us at: MochaCare Email: support@mochacare.com Website: www.mochacare.com MochaCare Backed by Y Combinator Your team for home care scheduling, interviewing, and growth. Human-led, AI-powered, from San Francisco. Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions SMS Terms Contact Us","raw_cache_path":"/Users/veer/Documents/StartUp/customer_discovery/data/raw/research/mochacare-com/48d5035f4237984f.html","fetched_at":"2026-05-18T21:06:45.332265Z","success":true,"error":null,"metadata":{"discovered_via":"search","query_used":"site:mochacare.com jobs"}}],"coverage":{"homepage_found":true,"careers_found":true,"docs_found":false,"status_found":false,"blog_or_changelog_found":false,"github_found":false,"seed_metadata_found":true,"fallback_search_used":true,"total_successful_sources":4,"source_diversity_score":0.375,"confidence_cap":"high"},"trace":{"probes_attempted":["seed_metadata","homepage","known_links","careers","docs","status","blog_changelog","github","agent_search_fallback"],"urls_attempted":["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/mochacare","https://www.mochacare.com","https://www.mochacare.com/sms-terms","https://www.mochacare.com/privacy","https://www.mochacare.com/sms-terms"],"failures":[],"cache_hits":0,"tool_calls":16}}
